  <text>
    <body>
      <div coords="1,50,450,500,300"><head>Introduction</head><p>Large language models often produce fluent but unsupported statements when asked about research papers. Prior work on retrieval <ref type="bibr" target="#b0">[1]</ref> and on citation grounding <ref type="bibr" target="#b2">[3]</ref> motivates our approach.</p></div>
      <div coords="2,50,100,500,300"><head>Related Work</head><p>Dense retrieval methods <ref type="bibr" target="#b1">[2]</ref> and hybrid search <ref type="bibr" target="#b2">[3]</ref> have both been used to build assistants that answer questions over large collections of scientific documents with references.</p></div>
